From 5592a073c7bb26db576cc7d674e6c97742d8ef3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:57:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(app): the workholding rpm table asserts all 24 cells

The walk in every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict
asserted 15 of its 24 cells. The 9 it skipped are the creation refusals:
turning work on a mill (none/mill x Work) and milling work on a plain
lathe (lathe x Tool). Each is now asserted refused at creation, by its
message; every other cell must be created and judged as before.

A new pin reaches the work_speed arm for a milling section on a plain
lathe through program_problems_by: over the chuck it is named, at the
limit it is clean. Through post() the family clause refuses it first.
No product code changes.

Fixes #1215

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
